# GitHub Code Owners
# This file defines who should review changes to specific areas of the codebase
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for all files in repository
* @security-team @devops-team

# Security-related files
.github/ @security-team
SECURITY.md @security-team
.github/workflows/codeql-analysis.yml @security-team @devops-team
.github/workflows/dependency-review.yml @security-team @devops-team
.github/workflows/security-orchestration.yml @security-team @devops-team
.github/codeql-config.yml @security-team
.github/secret_scanning.yml @security-team
.github/dependabot.yml @security-team
.github/IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md @security-team

# Application code
src/auth/ @security-team @backend-team
src/api/ @api-team
src/database/ @database-team @security-team
src/encryption/ @security-team @cryptography-team
src/logging/ @devops-team @security-team

# Infrastructure
docker/ @devops-team @security-team
terraform/ @devops-team @security-team
kubernetes/ @devops-team @security-team

# Configuration files
*.yml @security-team
*.yaml @security-team
.env.* @security-team
secrets.* @security-team

# Documentation
docs/ @tech-writers @security-team
README.md @project-leads
CONTRIBUTING.md @security-team @project-leads

# Build and dependency files
package.json @backend-team
package-lock.json @backend-team
requirements.txt @backend-team
requirements*.txt @backend-team
Pipfile @backend-team
pom.xml @backend-team
build.gradle @backend-team
Dockerfile @devops-team @security-team
docker-compose.yml @devops-team @security-team

# Test files
tests/ @qa-team
test/ @qa-team
__tests__/ @qa-team

# Configuration
.github/CODEOWNERS @security-team @project-leads
.gitignore @security-team
.gitattributes @security-team

# Notes:
# - A review from someone in the security-team is required for security-related changes
# - A review from devops-team is required for infrastructure changes
# - Multiple owners can be assigned (space-separated)
# - Teams should be written as @org-name/team-name or individual users as @username
# - More specific patterns override less specific ones
